+Before encoding, the P25 voice path applies a fixed 12 dB (4x) PCM calibration, then the microphone gain. Above a
+knee at 3/4 scale a limiter compresses peaks 4:1 toward full scale, with saturation only past it: the calibration
+alone puts a strong vowel over full scale, and the flat top a hard clip left there was audible as strain in the
+transmitted audio. The previous level was about 14 dB below the pinned Yazev IMBE reference encoder on the same
+harmonic signal. With the calibration, the transmitted frames decoded through both that reference and mbelib
+measured within 2.2 dB of the reference encoder's level. This is a transmit-input calibration only: the decoder and
+its golden vectors are unchanged. YSF VW uses the same voice path, calibration and limiter. The microphone setting
+remains 2 dB per step around step 5.
 
